  <h3>Keep it fresh: two clocks</h3>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="clock"><h4><span class="pill" style="background:#dbeafe;color:#1e3a8a">Code clock</span> on every push to main, or nightly</h4><ol>
      <li><code>git fetch</code>, then <code>git diff --name-status &lt;head_sha&gt; origin/main</code>.</li>
      <li>Re-parse only the changed files. MERGE their symbols and drop vanished ones.</li>
      <li>Refresh those files' outgoing edges, and re-resolve calls from files that import them.</li>
      <li>Re-summarise and re-embed only nodes whose <code>content_hash</code> changed.</li>
      <li>Recompute derived edges and fan-in/fan-out. Recompute communities weekly.</li>
      <li>Set <code>Repository.head_sha</code> and <code>indexed_at</code>.</li></ol></div>
    <div class="clock"><h4><span class="pill" style="background:#fee2e2;color:#7f1d1d">Status clock</span> every 10–15 min, or on webhooks</h4><ol>
      <li>Per repo: newest workflow runs on main, plus deployments and statuses per environment.</li>
      <li>MERGE <code>WorkflowRun</code> and <code>Deployment</code> nodes and their edges.</li>
      <li>Update roll-ups: <code>Repository.ci_status</code>, <code>Environment.current_sha</code>, <code>Workflow.success_rate_30d</code>.</li>
      <li>Delete runs older than the retention window (for example 30 days).</li>
      <li>Webhooks to subscribe to at org level: <code>push</code>, <code>workflow_run</code>, <code>deployment</code>, <code>deployment_status</code>.</li></ol></div>
  </div>
  <div class="callout why"><strong>Built: <code>c8_refresh.py</code>, scheduled in Windows Task Scheduler</strong>Every 30 minutes (task <code>codekg-refresh</code>) it compares each repo's branch heads with <code>git ls-remote</code>, which takes about 50 s when nothing moved, and re-indexes only repos whose branch moved. Every night at 02:00 (<code>codekg-refresh-nightly</code>) it also re-reads CI, deployments, PRs, teams and new or removed repos for the whole org.
    A changed repo is re-extracted in memory, which takes seconds, so callers in importing files are re-resolved too. Only the delta is written: changed nodes are MERGEd, vanished ones DETACH DELETEd, and only changed edges are replaced. Summaries and embeddings stay on unchanged nodes.
    <b>Tested</b> by rolling <code>cdp-genai-qrc-language-translation-be</code> back 3 commits and letting the refresh bring it forward. The 17 changed files gave 138 nodes added, 238 rewritten and 346 edges created, and only 164 of 23,556 nodes were re-embedded. The repository came back node-for-node identical. Webhooks would need GitHub to reach this machine, so the status clock is the nightly re-read plus the chatbot's live <code>github_live</code> tool.</div>
  <div class="callout why"><strong>You've built this pattern before</strong>Module 5P's sync did three moves: embed only new or changed rows, refresh cheap metadata, delete orphans. The code clock does the same thing per file.</div>
</div>
